A||||4||mshill||3.4L pushrod identification...||||1||
Z||000000||mshill||11-10-2000||12:29 PM||||I got my a 95 3.4L engine from a local auto recylceler (sp?).  Is there anything in the casting that would identify it as a 3.4L engine (as opposed to a 2.8L)?<P>It has a big "F" on either side and a serial (or casting) number on the front just above the timing cover.  Those are the only distiguishing marks on the block.<P>BTW, it is supposed to have 49K miles on it and when I removed the intake and valve covers the pushrods and rocker arms were just slightly bronzed with oil.  It looks like it was very well maintained. I am still debating if I should throw 1.6:1 rolloer rockers onto the top end.||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||11-10-2000||04:20 PM||||The 3.4's do have an F in the block, so it sounds like you have the right motor.  There should also be a plug stiking out of the pan....this isn't needed, but another distinguishing mark of a 3.4.    ||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||11-10-2000||05:01 PM||||The sides of the block have ribs in the casting and the 2.8/3.1-liter engines have smooth sides. This was to beef up the block for the larger bore. Also the starter holes are on the opposite side with the rear drive Camaro engine.<P>The 1.6 rockers won't give you much of an improvement. They will give you about a 1-5 horsepower difference according to dyno2000.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||11-10-2000||06:29 PM||||Thanks guys.  The "F" on the side and the plug in the oil pan as well as the ribs in the side of the block.  Sounds good.  Looks like I got the right engine.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||11-10-2000||09:10 PM||||I heard that the 1.6 ratio rocker arms will cause premature valve guide seal wear.  I would just go with 1.5 ratio roller rocker arms from Summit or Jegs.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
